From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:11:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt6351-fuel-gauge: report discharging with no
 supply online

The status came from the measured current alone, with a 20 mA band
reported as not charging. Unplugged, a current inside that band, or a
current register that reads near zero, then reported not charging, and
UPower took the battery to be waiting on a charger: a desktop showed it
as plugged in.

Inside the band, report not charging only while some supply is online,
and discharging otherwise. A battery held at a charge limit with the
charger attached still reads not charging.
---
 drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
index 63cbfa375..bfdefd105 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
@@ -44,7 +44,10 @@
 #define MT6351_FG_CHARGE_NAH		44983
 #define MT6351_FG_SENSE_BASE_MOHM	20
 
-/* Within this current, the battery is reported as not charging. */
+/*
+ * Within this current, the battery is reported as not charging while a supply
+ * is online, and as discharging otherwise.
+ */
 #define MT6351_FG_IDLE_UA		20000
 
 struct mt6351_fg {
@@ -185,6 +188,9 @@ static int mt6351_fg_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_MIN_DESIGN:
 		val->intval = fg->info->voltage_min_design_uv;
 		return 0;
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_SCOPE:
+		/* Asked of every supply when the core looks for one online. */
+		return -EINVAL;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
@@ -203,7 +209,7 @@ static int mt6351_fg_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS:
 		if (ua > MT6351_FG_IDLE_UA)
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
-		else if (ua < -MT6351_FG_IDLE_UA)
+		else if (ua < -MT6351_FG_IDLE_UA || power_supply_is_system_supplied() <= 0)
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 		else
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
